### Area 3: the tracker, an order's timeline, the exceptions queue and the KPIs.
### Every answer is mock data built from the synthetic data and says so in
### meta.mock. Sign in first (see auth.http): REST Client keeps the cookies.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Sign in as Management, who may read all four.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/demo-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "MANAGEMENT" }

### The tracker, a page at a time. Sort by orderNo, customerName, orderDate, shipmentDate or amount.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tracker/orders?page=1&pageSize=10&sort=orderDate&direction=desc

### Only the overdue orders, found by a search.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tracker/orders?overdue=true&search=SO

### Only the orders at one status, or held by one role. The status code is in each row.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tracker/orders?status=sample-awaiting-payment

### Several statuses at once, as a step of the sales flow opens them.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tracker/orders?status=sample-short-stock,sample-pending-approval

### The open orders, and the orders with a document to confirm.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tracker/orders?open=true

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tracker/orders?documentToConfirm=true

### Open orders at each of the nine sales steps. They add up to openOrders.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tracker/flow

### The queue is the open exceptions unless asked. ALL keeps the resolved ones too.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exceptions?state=ALL
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tracker/orders?ownerRole=WAREHOUSE&pageSize=50

### One order's timeline: pick an order No. from the list above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tracker/orders/SO-0001

### The exceptions queue: the open ones, or ?state=RESOLVED for the history.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exceptions?page=1&pageSize=25
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/exceptions?state=RESOLVED

### Spectra's five measures, as mock lab estimates, with twelve weekly values and a target each.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/insights/kpis
